                        "form": "gonfalon"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "34a93634-c696-3d21-a20c-1719de102fcd",
                        "entry_id": "7f1a5822-d32a-3141-9c82-9c1bcdb77971",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Bannière à plusieurs fanons."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "45fd4fe9-bf33-4e32-9c2b-c06f15a42408",
                                "sense_id": "34a93634-c696-3d21-a20c-1719de102fcd",
                                "text": "Il la faisait précéder par ses timbaliers, son parasol et son gonfanon, ses fusiliers et ses porte-glaives, contraignait ses seigneurs et cavaliers de marque à former son escorte, et ses bandes de rondeliers d’élite à la suivre, centeniers et joueurs de flûte en tête."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "55c951a1-8f0d-3a84-b779-4e6e979e71ac",
                        "entry_id": "7f1a5822-d32a-3141-9c82-9c1bcdb77971",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Meuble représentant la bannière du même nom dans les armoiries. Elle est généralement représentée à trois fanons et surmontée de trois cercles représentant les ancrages. Quand sa bordure est d'un autre émail, on le dit frangé. À rapprocher de bannière, étendard, guidon, oriflamme, pavillon et pennon."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b1db4d91-1e4d-47f9-b0d3-306428c16ebf",
                                "sense_id": "55c951a1-8f0d-3a84-b779-4e6e979e71ac",
                                "text": "D’or au gonfanon de gueules frangé de sinople, qui est de la région Auvergne → voir illustration « armoiries avec un gonfanon »"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3ab2d7ad-e497-4d76-8aff-0be98df08eb5",
                        "source_entry_id": "7f1a5822-d32a-3141-9c82-9c1bcdb77971",
                        "source_sense_description": "voir gonfalon",
                        "target_lang_word": "gonfanon",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8dab9773-c1e2-4526-a004-3c971606e311",
                        "source_entry_id": "7f1a5822-d32a-3141-9c82-9c1bcdb77971",
                        "source_sense_description": "voir gonfalon",
                        "target_lang_word": "gonfalon",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gonfalon",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "64f02cc1-320a-3d36-a179-5837c4e9d008",
                                        "entry_id": "129e4b0c-4889-3a40-b989-e36d284a196c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A standard or ensign, consisting of a pole with a crosspiece from which a banner is suspended, especially as used in church processions, but also for civic and military display."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ef7c4d5-17fb-442e-8170-4f3cf0373b8f",
                                                "sense_id": "64f02cc1-320a-3d36-a179-5837c4e9d008",
                                                "text": "Ten thousand thousand Ensignes high advanc'd,\nStandards, and Gonfalons twixt Van and Reare\nStreame in the Aire, and for distinction serve"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "914aec66-d6ea-4605-994f-4e7297f23c7a",
                                                "sense_id": "64f02cc1-320a-3d36-a179-5837c4e9d008",
                                                "text": "Ruthlessly pricking our gonfalon bubble,\nMaking a Giant hit into a double—\nWords that are heavy with nothing but trouble:\n“Tinker to Evers to Chance.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51f65145-5454-4f8e-9cbb-45904655502c",
                                                "sense_id": "64f02cc1-320a-3d36-a179-5837c4e9d008",
                                                "text": "With vermilion leaf or bronze—\nTatters of gorgeous gonfalons—"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d061913d-77e0-4a6c-891f-11dda2974d91",
                                                "sense_id": "64f02cc1-320a-3d36-a179-5837c4e9d008",
                                                "text": "It was in the queer little Church of Vera Cruz, beneath the castle, that the Knights Templar performed their secret rites of chivalry, standing vigil over their arms all night, in all the mysterious splendour of seneschal, gonfalon, and accolade."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7e0e6d4-63ae-348e-9eed-a949b86148b1",
                                        "entry_id": "129e4b0c-4889-3a40-b989-e36d284a196c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of gonfanon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
